{# THE MATRIX'S SHARED VOCABULARY.

   THE RENDERINGS TAKE THEIR MARKS FROM HERE for the reason the surface itself
   exists: they are several renderings of ONE declaration, and several copies of
   "how a concern is drawn" is several places for them to start disagreeing
   about it. The design app unrolls them because a static page has no other way
   to be looked at.

   IT USED TO DRAW A FLAT PERMISSION VALUE PER ROW, under an umbrella the
   catalogue invented. The ruling replaced that with the shape the declarations
   already have: ONE GROUP PER DECLARER, a ROW PER CONCERN, a COLUMN PER VERB,
   and a CELL ONLY WHERE THE CONCERN DECLARES THAT VERB — so there is never a
   checkbox that would mean nothing.

   THE STATE THAT OUTLIVES A MODULE lives here too — the ORPHANED GRANT — because
   every direction has to draw it and none of them may draw it differently. #}

{% macro icon_tick() %}<svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>{% endmacro %}
{% macro icon_info() %}<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>{% endmacro %}
{% macro icon_people() %}<svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>{% endmacro %}
{% macro icon_plus() %}<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="M12 5v14"/></svg>{% endmacro %}
{% macro icon_save() %}<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15.2 3a2 2 0 0 1 1.4.6l3.8 3.8a2 2 0 0 1 .6 1.4V19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z"/><path d="M17 21v-7a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H8a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v7"/><path d="M7 3v4a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h7"/></svg>{% endmacro %}
{% macro icon_warn() %}<svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3"/><path d="M12 9v4"/><path d="M12 17h.01"/></svg>{% endmacro %}

{# THE GROUP HEADING, WEARING ITS DECLARER. Whoever enforces a concern declares
   it, and the heading says so in that package's own words — so an administrator
   reading a row can see which package gave it to them, and which package
   removing would take it away. This page never invents a name for somebody
   else's bundle: the word printed is the one `declaredBy()` returned. #}
{% macro group_head(declarer, pairs, held) %}
    {%- set on = pairs|filter(p => p in held)|length -%}
    <div class="pm-umb">
        <b>{{ declarer }}</b>
        <span class="pm-by"><i></i>declared by {{ declarer }}</span>
        {# SELECT ALL, AS A PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT. The design draws the count
           as a button that ticks the whole group; it ships DISABLED and the
           Stimulus controller's connect() is what makes it live, so it is a
           control exactly when there is behaviour behind it and reads as the
           plain count it has always been when there is not. Nothing here
           writes: the boxes change, and Save is still the only thing that
           saves. See assets/controllers/permission_group_controller.js. #}
        <button type="button" class="pm-all" style="margin-left:auto" disabled
                data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--permission-group-target="all"
                data-action="uhifadhi--team-bundle--permission-group#toggle"><span class="a">all</span> <span class="c">{{ on }} of {{ pairs|length }}</span></button>
    </div>
{% endmacro %}

{# THE SIX VERBS, AS THE COLUMN HEADS. Fixed in the contracts so a module
   cannot invent a seventh, and drawn in every group in the same order — a
   matrix whose columns differ per group is a matrix nobody can read across.
   Each head carries its own sentence, because the person handing the power
   over is the one who needs to know what "manage" covers. #}
{% macro verb_heads(verbs) %}
    <tr>
        <th class="pm-rowh"><span class="lbl" style="margin:0">resource</span></th>
        {% for verb in verbs %}
            <th class="pm-verbh" title="{{ verb.meaning }}">{{ verb.label }}</th>
        {% endfor %}
    </tr>
{% endmacro %}

{# THE ROW'S NAME: the concern's label, the key a route and a grant name it by,
   and the one sentence that says what it is about — the whole point of a
   description being required at declaration.

   A SENSITIVE CONCERN IS MARKED. It is a fact about a person or about a case
   that an organization may reasonably want withheld without withholding the
   page it sits on, and an administrator ticking `manage` on it should be told
   that before the click rather than after. #}
{% macro concern_name(concern) %}
    <div class="pm-name">
        <b>{{ concern.label }}{% if concern.isSensitive %}<span class="pm-sens">sensitive</span>{% endif %}</b>
        <span class="perm">{{ concern.key }}</span>
        <em>{{ concern.description }}</em>
    </div>
{% endmacro %}

{# ONE CELL. A CONCERN AND A VERB, TOGETHER — and nothing at all where the
   concern does not declare the verb, because a box that would mean nothing is
   worse than a gap a reader can see.

   §5.6(c): a bounded administrator may grant only what their own position
   holds. `grantable` is that list of pairs (null = unbounded, everything
   grantable); a cell outside it is drawn disabled, so the fence is visible. A
   pair the position already holds beyond the admin's reach stays
   ticked-but-frozen — the controller keeps it, the admin cannot touch it. #}
{% macro cell(concern, verb, held, grantable = null, editable = true) %}
    {% import _self as pm %}
    {%- if not concern.supports(verb) -%}
        <td class="pm-nocell"><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="vh">{{ concern.label }} declares no {{ verb.label|lower }}</span></td>
    {%- else -%}
        {%- set pair = concern.key ~ '.' ~ verb.value -%}
        {%- set on = pair in held -%}
        {%- set can = grantable is null or pair in grantable -%}
        <td>
            {%- if editable -%}
                <label class="pm-box{{ on ? ' on' : '' }}{{ can ? '' : ' pm-locked' }}"
                       title="{{ pair }}{{ can ? '' : ' — beyond your authority: your own position does not hold it' }}">
                    <input type="checkbox" class="pm-check" name="grants[]" value="{{ pair }}"{{ on ? ' checked' : '' }}{{ can ? ' ' : ' disabled' }}
                           data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--permission-group-target="box"
                           aria-label="{{ concern.label }} — {{ verb.label }}">
                    <i>{{ pm.icon_tick() }}</i>
                </label>
            {%- else -%}
                <span class="pm-box pm-ro{{ on ? ' on' : '' }}" title="{{ pair }}"><i>{{ pm.icon_tick() }}</i></span>
            {%- endif -%}
        </td>
    {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{# A POSITION THAT GRANTS NOTHING SAYS SO IN THOSE WORDS. It is the model's
   zero rather than a fault or a blank screen: somebody holding it can sign in
   and reach nothing behind it. #}
{% macro grants_nothing() %}
    {% import _self as pm %}
    <p class="pm-nobody">{{ pm.icon_info() }} This position grants nothing. Somebody holding it can sign in and reach no page behind it &mdash; tick a cell to change that.</p>
{% endmacro %}

{# AN ORPHANED GRANT — still in a position's JSON, declared by nothing.

   PRUNE, NOT PURGE. Uninstalling a module leaves the pairs behind and stops
   them resolving; removing them would have silently rewritten what somebody
   granted. So they are drawn MUTED and ticked, and unticking one still works,
   because it is a grant rather than a fixture.

   THE TICKED BOX IS LOAD-BEARING: it is what makes a save that does not touch
   the orphan keep it, since the form posts only what is ticked. #}
{% macro orphans(values, held) %}
    {% import _self as pm %}
    {%- set mine = values|filter(v => v in held) -%}
    {% if mine|length %}
        <div class="pm-group pm-mod-orphan">
            <div class="pm-umb pm-mod-orphan">
                <b>No longer declared</b>
                <span class="pm-by next"><i></i>nothing installed declares these</span>
            </div>
            {% for value in mine %}
                <label class="pm-row on muted">
                    <input type="checkbox" name="grants[]" value="{{ value }}" checked class="pm-check">
                    <span class="pm-tick">{{ pm.icon_tick() }}</span>
                    <span class="pm-t">
                        <b><span class="pm-orphname">no longer described</span></b>
                        <span class="perm">{{ value }}</span>
                        <em>This position still holds it and <b>no installed module declares it</b> &mdash; the
                        bundle that declared it has been removed. It is kept rather than deleted, because
                        uninstalling a module must not silently rewrite what somebody granted. It resolves to
                        nothing today, and it will start working again if that module comes back. Untick it to
                        take it away for good.</em>
                    </span>
                    <span></span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
